(3462709, 479323, 66384, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites. I gave it a 9. That toy in the cradle doesn''t look quite like it belongs, but I figured this was some sort of museum room, so you couldn''t do anything about that. But I think it hurts the composition. Nice lighting, and I don''t mind the highlight on the bed.</td>', 'This was one of my favorites. I gave it a 9. That toy in the cradle doesn''t look quite like it belongs, but I figured this was some sort of museum room, so you couldn''t do anything about that. But I think it hurts the composition. Nice lighting, and I don''t mind the highlight on the bed.', '2007-03-14 23:16:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3462733, 477379, 66384, '<td valign="top">This is a really interesting design. I didn''t quite know what to make of it -- I was so involved with trying to understand where you were when you took it.</td>', 'This is a really interesting design. I didn''t quite know what to make of it -- I was so involved with trying to understand where you were when you took it.', '2007-03-14 23:30:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3463300, 475494, 58473, '<td valign="top">Great shot . Beauty clouds. Congrats on top 5.</td>', 'Great shot . Beauty clouds. Congrats on top 5.', '2007-03-15 04:43:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3463315, 479147, 57229, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments (both before <u>and</u> after).<br/>According to the file numbers, I reeled off about 19 shots at this lot, most of which involved bouncing a flash off a white umbrella. When I got round to processing, I saw how dead the flashlight was, albeit even.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=484369" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/484369.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/484369.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/484369.jpg"/></a> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=484374" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/484374.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/484374.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/484374.jpg"/></a> <br/>The cat, of course, popped up entirely according to his own whim. I liked the idea of including the stove as a complementary framing element, but nothing could justify the inclusion of the space between the stove and the sofa. Funny, that.<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments (both before and after).According to the file numbers, I reeled off about 19 shots at this lot, most of which involved bouncing a flash off a white umbrella. When I got round to processing, I saw how dead the flashlight was, albeit even.  The cat, of course, popped up entirely according to his own whim. I liked the idea of including the stove as a complementary framing element, but nothing could justify the inclusion of the space between the stove and the sofa. Funny, that.', '2007-03-15 05:12:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3463473, 478299, 18450, '<td valign="top">Simply stunning abstract image Shez!!!</td>', 'Simply stunning abstract image Shez!!!', '2007-03-15 07:56:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3463481, 478446, 56744, '<td valign="top">This is great photo, eye-catching on so many levels, lighting, composition and creativity. The use of red color and tone are fantastic. Could be a winner in the RED challenge too ;)<br/> <br/>I wish you could explain how you did this terrific light. Congrats!!!<br/></td>', 'This is great photo, eye-catching on so many levels, lighting, composition and creativity. The use of red color and tone are fantastic. Could be a winner in the RED challenge too ;) I wish you could explain how you did this terrific light. Congrats!!!', '2007-03-15 08:04:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3463484, 479311, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>A very creative take on this challenge.  This is the first image I''ve critiqued where the number of 6 votes was higher than the number of 5 votes and the final score was below a 6.  I think there are two primary reasons this image didn''t score higher.  First, the image lacks contrast and looks a little flat.  With advanced editing, it would have been relatively easy to process the boys separately from the chair to bring out the best of both.  Second, the perspective of this image, in combination with the low contrast, provides very little separation between the boys and the chair, making the image look very two-dimensional.  I think you found the perfect prop for this challenge but needed to play around a bit more compositionally to find "the" image.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, A very creative take on this challenge.  This is the first image I''ve critiqued where the number of 6 votes was higher than the number of 5 votes and the final score was below a 6.  I think there are two primary reasons this image didn''t score higher.  First, the image lacks contrast and looks a little flat.  With advanced editing, it would have been relatively easy to process the boys separately from the chair to bring out the best of both.  Second, the perspective of this image, in combination with the low contrast, provides very little separation between the boys and the chair, making the image look very two-dimensional.  I think you found the perfect prop for this challenge but needed to play around a bit more compositionally to find "the" image. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2007-03-15 08:07:11.000000', NULL, 0),
