(3465211, 478187, 1024, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>I wrote you a very long and detailed critique, but the demons in my computer ate it, so lets start again.<br/> <br/>This image has a few strengths,  The symetry is wonderful, not only in the brick work, the columns and the piers, but also in the trees fading into the distance.  Its almost like a mirror image.  The scene is very tranquil, from the ripples on the water it appears that there is a slight breeze blowing.  It is a very calming photograph.<br/> <br/> <br/>This photograph meets the challenge. It works, but not at the highest levels viewers may be looking for.  The voters want to be challenged.  They want to see a photograph that makes they wonder how you could have captured such an image.  Your colors seem muted.  There is nothing here that draws the eye and shouts "I am the subject of this photo".  Perhaps if you had a brightly dressed person, maybe even a child, sitting on the bench or leaning against one of the pillers.<br/> <br/>From the scores this photo received (no 1''s or 2''s, and also no 9''s or 10''s) it seems that no one loved or hated it.  It is a difficult photo to be passionate about in either direction.<br/> <br/>This critique is just my humbnle opinion, and I hope you found it helpful in some small way.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club: I wrote you a very long and detailed critique, but the demons in my computer ate it, so lets start again. This image has a few strengths,  The symetry is wonderful, not only in the brick work, the columns and the piers, but also in the trees fading into the distance.  Its almost like a mirror image.  The scene is very tranquil, from the ripples on the water it appears that there is a slight breeze blowing.  It is a very calming photograph.  This photograph meets the challenge. It works, but not at the highest levels viewers may be looking for.  The voters want to be challenged.  They want to see a photograph that makes they wonder how you could have captured such an image.  Your colors seem muted.  There is nothing here that draws the eye and shouts "I am the subject of this photo".  Perhaps if you had a brightly dressed person, maybe even a child, sitting on the bench or leaning against one of the pillers. From the scores this photo received (no 1''s or 2''s, and also no 9''s or 10''s) it seems that no one loved or hated it.  It is a difficult photo to be passionate about in either direction. This critique is just my humbnle opinion, and I hope you found it helpful in some small way.', '2007-03-15 20:51:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3466160, 479190, 66384, '<td valign="top">I love your bed and quilt, and the cat is beautiful. The whole composition comes together very nicely, and the light gives the photo a lovely morning mood. (Seems too early in the morning for the bed to be made up.) The object(s) on the nightstand cast a nice shadow that is good for the composition, but I find them distracting because I can''t tell what they are.</td>', 'I love your bed and quilt, and the cat is beautiful. The whole composition comes together very nicely, and the light gives the photo a lovely morning mood. (Seems too early in the morning for the bed to be made up.) The object(s) on the nightstand cast a nice shadow that is good for the composition, but I find them distracting because I can''t tell what they are.', '2007-03-16 08:56:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3466167, 478119, 66384, '<td valign="top">I like the colors and the tone of this image. The fire in the stove is very inviting. With the tightness of the setup, there doesn''t seem to be room for anyone to sit and relax, and the chair is not inviting since it has the lace on the seat and is already full of objects. Also the back of the chair is too the fire, which seem unnatural. I think there is too much here. Either a cozy inviting scene, or just the still life with the chair and objects might have worked better.</td>', 'I like the colors and the tone of this image. The fire in the stove is very inviting. With the tightness of the setup, there doesn''t seem to be room for anyone to sit and relax, and the chair is not inviting since it has the lace on the seat and is already full of objects. Also the back of the chair is too the fire, which seem unnatural. I think there is too much here. Either a cozy inviting scene, or just the still life with the chair and objects might have worked better.', '2007-03-16 09:07:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3466177, 479356, 66384, '<td valign="top">The lighting is beautiful and completely conveys the feel of a quiet reading retreat. I don''t like the pink book in the chair. but I agree there needs to be something in the chair to appeal to the viewer, e.g.a small child reading in a large chair, because the chair itself isn''t very interesting.</td>', 'The lighting is beautiful and completely conveys the feel of a quiet reading retreat. I don''t like the pink book in the chair. but I agree there needs to be something in the chair to appeal to the viewer, e.g.a small child reading in a large chair, because the chair itself isn''t very interesting.', '2007-03-16 09:16:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3467507, 479305, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Seen better days"  is a good entry into the furniture challenge.  I was peaking around on your info and see a very similar photo in the Free Study challenge, I think I like this one the best.  <br/> <br/>You have found an interesting subject and created a good composition in the frame.  I like that you brought the colors out to grab the viewers eye.  I think you did a good job of leaving the wall in the background to show the environment and that this was not just a set up for a photo.  The lighting looks pretty good, like maybe you were using natural light.  the only thing I can really see that might need some adjusting is the focus on the lower left side towards the corner of the seat.  <br/> <br/>Overall I think you did an extremely good job in a tough challenge.  I really look forward to your future entries, you have a good eye. <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Seen better days"  is a good entry into the furniture challenge.  I was peaking around on your info and see a very similar photo in the Free Study challenge, I think I like this one the best.   You have found an interesting subject and created a good composition in the frame.  I like that you brought the colors out to grab the viewers eye.  I think you did a good job of leaving the wall in the background to show the environment and that this was not just a set up for a photo.  The lighting looks pretty good, like maybe you were using natural light.  the only thing I can really see that might need some adjusting is the focus on the lower left side towards the corner of the seat.   Overall I think you did an extremely good job in a tough challenge.  I really look forward to your future entries, you have a good eye. ', '2007-03-16 21:54:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3467595, 478993, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Mueblador de Mexico" is a good entry into the furniture challenge because it shows up the creation of the furniture.  Great job seeing this opportunity and being able to capture it. <br/> <br/>The image looks technically very clean.  I like the natural lighting, it makes the image feel very much like it was not staged.   I think the composition works for this piece.  I would be curious to see the shot with his feet left in the shot and a little more cropped out of the top.  The focus looks good, we are defiantly looking at our subject the chair and its creator.  <br/> <br/>Nice work.  <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Mueblador de Mexico" is a good entry into the furniture challenge because it shows up the creation of the furniture.  Great job seeing this opportunity and being able to capture it.  The image looks technically very clean.  I like the natural lighting, it makes the image feel very much like it was not staged.   I think the composition works for this piece.  I would be curious to see the shot with his feet left in the shot and a little more cropped out of the top.  The focus looks good, we are defiantly looking at our subject the chair and its creator.   Nice work.  ', '2007-03-16 22:42:46.000000', NULL, 0),
